From: lane L5b (wave580), 2026-10-25
Subject: Carry `peer_mesh` from the root's execution_nodes map into the execution-node module

The execution-node module (unprotected, landed in this lane's branch) now
takes a `peer_mesh` variable, renders QIP_PEER_MESH_LISTEN, QIP_PEER_MESH_PEERS
and QIP_PEER_MESH_CLOCK_BOUND_MS into node.env when it is set, opens the
firewall both ways for exactly the peers named, and refuses at plan every
value the binary would refuse at start (tests/peer-mesh.tftest.hcl, 10 runs).
Without this patch nothing can set it: the root's `execution_nodes` object
type has no `peer_mesh` field, and adding one is an edit to
infrastructure/terraform/variables.tf, which is protected, so the root's
main.tf line that would pass it cannot land alone either (terraform validate
refuses an unknown attribute). The dev tfvars entry (also protected) gains
`peer_mesh = null` so the choice is visible where a reviewer reads it.

What the patch does not do: declare a second node or a peer address. Both are
billed infrastructure declined by decision 5 of 2026-10-25, and a peer's
address must be stable, which a managed instance group's machine is not
(see the module variable's description). The patch adds a gate and a field
whose default leaves every environment exactly as it was; it weakens
nothing (decision 3 of 2026-10-25). Apply with
`git apply docs/blueprint/lanes/l5b-peer-mesh-root.patch`, then run
`terraform fmt -check`, `terraform validate` and
`cargo test -p qip-acceptance --test infrastructure --test terraform_contract --test manifest_wiring`.

diff --git a/infrastructure/terraform/variables.tf b/infrastructure/terraform/variables.tf
--- a/infrastructure/terraform/variables.tf
+++ b/infrastructure/terraform/variables.tf
@@ -355,6 +355,23 @@
     # list that decides that, and the binary refuses a declaration naming a
     # venue outside it rather than adding one.
     cross_region_mirror_path = optional(string, "")
+    # ADR 0116: the peer Reflex Mesh this node joins, or null for a node that
+    # coordinates with no other cell directly — which is every node, because
+    # a peer needs a stable address and whatever fronts a managed instance
+    # group's machine with one is billed infrastructure declined by decision
+    # 5 of 2026-10-25. The module validates every field against what
+    # `qip-edge-node` would refuse at start (modules/execution-node, variable
+    # `peer_mesh`), and renders the three QIP_PEER_MESH_* lines only when this
+    # is set. Null here cannot be mistaken for an empty mesh: the module
+    # refuses a map naming no peer.
+    peer_mesh = optional(object({
+      listen_port    = number
+      clock_bound_ms = optional(number)
+      peers = map(object({
+        address = string
+        port    = number
+      }))
+    }))
   }))
 
   default = {}
diff --git a/infrastructure/terraform/main.tf b/infrastructure/terraform/main.tf
--- a/infrastructure/terraform/main.tf
+++ b/infrastructure/terraform/main.tf
@@ -767,6 +767,10 @@
   # a property of where that cell sits, not of the environment. Empty is every
   # venue at home, which is what every node has run as.
   cross_region_mirror_path = each.value.cross_region_mirror_path
+  # ADR 0116: null for every declared node until a peer has a stable address
+  # (modules/execution-node/README.md, "The peer mesh is declared here and is
+  # null everywhere").
+  peer_mesh = each.value.peer_mesh
 
   # Per node and never defaulted; see the variable's own description.
   region_allocation = each.value.region_allocation
diff --git a/infrastructure/environments/dev/terraform.tfvars b/infrastructure/environments/dev/terraform.tfvars
--- a/infrastructure/environments/dev/terraform.tfvars
+++ b/infrastructure/environments/dev/terraform.tfvars
@@ -263,6 +263,10 @@
     # what the node trades, and the binary refuses at start-up a declaration
     # naming a venue outside `venues` above.
     cross_region_mirror_path = ""
+    # ADR 0116: no peer. A second node and the stable address that fronts
+    # each peer are billed (decision 5 of 2026-10-25); the module refuses a
+    # mesh naming no peer, so null is the only honest value until then.
+    peer_mesh = null
   }
 }
 
